            <ArticleTitle>Cough in asthma triggered by reflux episodes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>143-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With combined pH and impedance monitoring, non-acid, as well as acid reflux episodes, are more commonly detected immediately prior to cough in asthma in children. Gastroesophageal reflux should be evaluated as a trigger for cough in difficult childhood asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
